{"name":"Globe Thistle","hex":"#2e0329","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"globe thistle","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of the flowering plants in the genus Echinops, with spiny foliage and blue or white spherical flower heads."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/globe_thistle"}],"entries":[{"title":"Echinops","blocks":[{"text":"Echinops is a genus of about 130 species of flowering plants in the family Asteraceae, commonly known as globe thistles. They have spiny foliage and produce blue or white spherical flower heads. They are distributed from central Asia, Mongolia and north-eastern China to the Mediterranean basin, temperate regions of Eurasia, reaching to Indian subcontinent and tropical Africa. Globe thistles are a common host plant for weevils of the genus Larinus."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/da/Fuzzy-horned_bumblebee_%28Bombus_mixtus%29_on_globe_thistle_%28Echinops_sp.%29_Seward_Park.jpg/330px-Fuzzy-horned_bumblebee_%28Bombus_mixtus%29_on_globe_thistle_%28Echinops_sp.%29_Seward_Park.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Echinops","wikidata":"Q650106"},{"title":"Globe","blocks":[{"text":"A globe is a spherical model of Earth, of some other celestial body, or of the celestial sphere. Globes serve purposes similar to maps, but, unlike maps, they do not distort the surface that they portray except to scale it down. A model globe of Earth is called a terrestrial globe. A model globe of the celestial sphere is called a celestial globe."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/The_Great_Globe%2C_Guyot_Hall%2C_Princeton_University.jpg/330px-The_Great_Globe%2C_Guyot_Hall%2C_Princeton_University.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Globe","wikidata":"Q133792"},{"title":"Thistle","blocks":[{"text":"Thistle is the popular name of a group of flowering plants characterised by leaves with sharp spikes on the margins, mostly in the family Asteraceae. Prickles can also occur all over the plant – on the stem, and on the flat parts of the leaves. These prickles protect the plant from herbivores. Typically, an involucre with a clasping shape, similar to a cup or urn, subtends each of a thistle's flower heads. The typically feathery pappus of a ripe thistle flower is known as thistle-down."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/Carduus_Nutans_in_the_Carpathian_Mountains.jpg/330px-Carduus_Nutans_in_the_Carpathian_Mountains.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thistle","wikidata":"Q538906"},{"title":"Shades of purple","blocks":[{"text":"There are numerous variations of the color purple, a sampling of which is shown below."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Shades_of_Purple.svg/330px-Shades_of_Purple.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shades_of_purple","wikidata":"Q7460344"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/Illustration_Echinops_sphaerocephalus0.jpg/500px-Illustration_Echinops_sphaerocephalus0.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/Illustration_Echinops_sphaerocephalus0.jpg/1280px-Illustration_Echinops_sphaerocephalus0.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/Illustration_Echinops_sphaerocephalus0.jpg/500px-Illustration_Echinops_sphaerocephalus0.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Illustration of globe thistle Echinops sphaerocephalus","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AIllus